 "corpus_budget_seconds": 1200,
 "note": [
  "dataset_label is the EqBench directory lane (Eq / Neq).  It is NOT a",
  "ground truth: the semantic relation comes from ground_truth_file,",
  "which points at scripts/eqbench/neq_ground_truth.tsv (or at the",
  "eq_sample_single_source rule).  Nothing in this file reaches the",
  "checker; it is test metadata only.",
  "pr_gate selects the replays the per-PR gate runs (job recorded-fast).",
  "It is a scheduling decision, not a coverage one: every case runs in the",
  "recorded-full workflow, with the same validator and the same assertions.",
  "The two cases outside the gate are the ones that dominate the wall clock",
  "(wood and barthe2big, ~92 %); excluding them keeps the PR critical path",
  "short without weakening any case's checks.  Nothing may be dropped from",
  "the full corpus to make a budget fit.",
  "budget_seconds is applied as a real deadline: the replay worker's process",
  "group is killed when it expires, so a hung worker fails fast instead of",
  "running into the job timeout.  It guards one replay against a regression",
  "in the checker, not against a slow machine, so it comes from the SLOWEST",
  "measured environment (measured_seconds) with headroom, with a floor for",
  "the cheap cases.  A GitHub-hosted runner was 2.7x slower than the",
  "container on barthe2big, so a budget derived from the container alone",
  "would fail there for reasons that have nothing to do with the checker.",
  "Exceeding it is a test-harness failure and never becomes a production",
  "UNKNOWN or TIMEOUT outcome.",
  "corpus_budget_seconds is the Issue #109 time acceptance criterion as",
  "revised on 2026-09-17: 1200 s for ALL nine replays on a GitHub-hosted",
  "runner.  It is the SUM of the measured replay times, never the wall clock",
  "of a parallel workflow -- running the corpus as a matrix shortens the",
  "workflow but changes nothing about the criterion.  The original 180 s was",
  "a placeholder that the measurements disproved.  The corpus is not shrunk",
  "to fit a budget: cases are not dropped, recorded surface is not trimmed,",
  "and a harness timeout is never reported as an UNKNOWN."
 ],
